Align indirect callback function signatures with their caller typedefs under Fil-C

Fil-C enforces argument count/size and return type matching at indirect
call sites. PHP 5.6 casts several callbacks whose definitions disagree
with the target function pointer typedef (mostly fixed in PHP 8):

- sapi/cli/php_cli.c: print_extension_info took 2 args and returned int,
  while zend_llist_apply calls llist_apply_func_t (void (*)(void *)).
- sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_main.c and sapi/cgi/cgi_main.c: print_extension_info
  returned int while called via llist_apply_with_arg_func_t (void); align
  with PHP 8 to static void print_extension_info(zend_extension *ext) and
  zend_llist_apply().
- Zend/zend_builtin_functions.c: add_zendext_info returned int while
  called via llist_apply_with_arg_func_t (void).
- Zend/zend_generators.c: copy_closure_static_var returned void while
  called via apply_func_args_t (int).
- ext/libxml/libxml.c: _php_libxml_free_error returned int while called
  via llist_dtor_func_t (void).
- ext/gd/libgd/gd_jpeg.c: php_jpeg_emit_message returned long while
  assigned to void (*emit_message)(j_common_ptr, int).

